+## Deploy on Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-6B4EFF)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=Nutlope%2Fblinkshot)
+
+Wasmer detects Next.js, installs dependencies with pnpm (from `pnpm-lock.yaml`), runs `pnpm run build` (`next build`) and serves the production build with Node. The button builds this public repo as-is and does not fork or copy it; to customize the app (start with `app/page.tsx`) and redeploy on every push, fork it and connect your fork from the Wasmer dashboard. Set these in the app's Settings → Environment Vars:
+
+| Variable | Required | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `TOGETHER_API_KEY` | Yes | Image generation (also needed when visitors enter their own Together key) |
+| `HELICONE_API_KEY` | No | Sends requests through Helicone for observability |
+| `BRAINTRUST_API_KEY`, `BRAINTRUST_PROJECT` | No | Generation tracing (project defaults to `blinkshot`) |
+| `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL`, `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN` | No | Rate limiting (5 requests per IP per day without a user key); skipped when unset |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | No | Extra allowed origin for the API origin check |
+
